{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_015yBQoUkDbSPjpP4cDgbQxr","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ACL Rolling Review 2025 2026 review form overall assessment score 1-5 scale soundness novelty\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \\\"Publish or Perish\\\" Circus | CSPaper Forum\",\"url\":\"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection\",\"url\":\"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/\"},{\"title\":\"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing\"},{\"title\":\"ACLRollingReview (@ReviewAcl) / Posts / X\",\"url\":\"https://x.com/ReviewAcl\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Dashboard\",\"url\":\"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding the ACL Rolling Review 2025-2026 scoring system:\n\n## Review Scores\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Overall Assessment Score\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n## Scoring Context\n\nWhile the search results don't explicitly state the 1-5 scale in the official review form documentation, they do indicate that all papers recommended for Findings and main conferences are expected to be sufficiently sound and reproducible, but you may consider a paper worthy of the main conference even if you personally are not excited about it. For example, improvements in efficiency of some algorithm, or creating a high-quality resource for a language/domain that does not yet have resources of that type may not sound very novel or exciting, but you may still consider it a significant contribution due to its potential impact.\n\nThe official ACL Rolling Review website (aclrollingreview.org/reviewform) contains the actual review form, though the detailed scoring scale definitions were not fully captured in these search results.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2e9568a-8920-4443-b16c-735005e3494c","uuid":"2105994e-18a3-4f86-91e6-5fd86fb541d9","timestamp":"2026-05-13T10:03:10.745Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ACL Rolling Review 2025 2026 review form overall assessment score 1-5 scale soundness novelty","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01VhzG4bvULrY7ZABmQkd5pY","content":[{"title":"Review Form – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"🎪 ACL 2025 Reviews Are Out: To Rebut or Flee? The Harsh Reality of NLP’s \"Publish or Perish\" Circus | CSPaper Forum","url":"https://forum.cspaper.org/topic/27/acl-2025-reviews-are-out-to-rebut-or-flee-the-harsh-reality-of-nlp-s-publish-or-perish-circus"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ACL Rolling Review Data Collection (ARR-DC) - ARR Data Collection","url":"https://arr-data.aclweb.org/"},{"title":"How ARR works – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewing"},{"title":"ACLRollingReview (@ReviewAcl) / Posts / X","url":"https://x.com/ReviewAcl"},{"title":"ARR Dashboard","url":"https://stats.aclrollingreview.org/"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"CALL FOR PAPERS – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/cfp"}]},"Based on the search results, here's what I found regarding the ACL Rolling Review 2025-2026 scoring system:\n\n## Review Scores\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n## Overall Assessment Score\n\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n## Scoring Context\n\nWhile the search results don't explicitly state the 1-5 scale in the official review form documentation, they do indicate that all papers recommended for Findings and main conferences are expected to be sufficiently sound and reproducible, but you may consider a paper worthy of the main conference even if you personally are not excited about it. For example, improvements in efficiency of some algorithm, or creating a high-quality resource for a language/domain that does not yet have resources of that type may not sound very novel or exciting, but you may still consider it a significant contribution due to its potential impact.\n\nThe official ACL Rolling Review website (aclrollingreview.org/reviewform) contains the actual review form, though the detailed scoring scale definitions were not fully captured in these search results."],"durationSeconds":6.635050553000001}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01QAtF9c5LWKUSMwXjZcQQPm","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"ARR review form dimensions \"overall assessment\" \"soundness\" \"excitement\" scoring scale 2025\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Review Form\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Reviewer Guidelines\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines\"},{\"title\":\"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md\"},{\"title\":\"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics\",\"url\":\"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Policies - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-acl23/\"},{\"title\":\"ARR 2025 Statistics: February Track - Paper Copilot\",\"url\":\"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/arr-statistics/arr-2025-statistics-february-track/\"},{\"title\":\"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/\"},{\"title\":\"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}\",\"url\":\"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023\",\"url\":\"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I found comprehensive information about the ARR review form dimensions for 2025:\n\n## ARR Review Form Dimensions (2025)\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Three Scoring Dimensions:\n\n**1. Soundness**\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. Reviewers should assess whether the paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them. The soundness scoring scale includes:\n- 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type.\n- 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims. Some extra experiments could be nice, but not essential.\n- 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\n\n**2. Excitement**\nExcitement scores reflect our personal taste, and so do not necessarily come with explicit reasons. The excitement scale includes:\n- 5 = Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 4 = Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\n\n**3. Overall Assessment**\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f2e9568a-8920-4443-b16c-735005e3494c","uuid":"dad3ea85-b550-4231-8560-f59049080de7","timestamp":"2026-05-13T10:03:17.550Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"ARR review form dimensions \"overall assessment\" \"soundness\" \"excitement\" scoring scale 2025","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_011UfTACYNG8kT3rY3XYppDQ","content":[{"title":"Review Form","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewform"},{"title":"ARR Reviewer Guidelines","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/reviewerguidelines"},{"title":"ARR Area Chair Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/acguidelines"},{"title":"aclrollingreview/reviewerguidelines.md at main · acl-org/aclrollingreview","url":"https://github.com/acl-org/aclrollingreview/blob/main/reviewerguidelines.md"},{"title":"Authors Guidelines – ACL Rolling Review – A peer review platform for the Association for Computational Linguistics","url":"http://aclrollingreview.org/authors"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Policies - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-acl23/"},{"title":"ARR 2025 Statistics: February Track - Paper Copilot","url":"https://papercopilot.com/statistics/arr-statistics/arr-2025-statistics-february-track/"},{"title":"ACL 2023 Acceptance Recommendations - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/overall-recommendation/"},{"title":"Program Chairs’ Report on Peer Review at ACL 2023 Anna Rogers}","url":"https://aclanthology.org/2023.acl-long.report.pdf"},{"title":"ACL’23 Peer Review Form - ACL 2023","url":"https://2023.aclweb.org/blog/review-form/"}]},"Based on the search results, I found comprehensive information about the ARR review form dimensions for 2025:\n\n## ARR Review Form Dimensions (2025)\n\nStarting with February 2025, ARR reviewers are asked to provide three scores: soundness, excitement, and overall recommendation.\n\n### Three Scoring Dimensions:\n\n**1. Soundness**\nThe soundness scores must be justified by the text of the review. Reviewers should assess whether the paper is sufficiently sound and thorough, whether it clearly states scientific claims and provides adequate support for them. The soundness scoring scale includes:\n- 5 = Excellent: This study is one of the most thorough I have seen, given its type.\n- 4 = Strong: This study provides sufficient support for all of its claims. Some extra experiments could be nice, but not essential.\n- 3 = Acceptable: This study provides sufficient support for its main claims.\n\n**2. Excitement**\nExcitement scores reflect our personal taste, and so do not necessarily come with explicit reasons. The excitement scale includes:\n- 5 = Highly Exciting: I would recommend this paper to others and/or attend its presentation in a conference.\n- 4 = Exciting: I would mention this paper to others and/or make an effort to attend its presentation in a conference.\n\n**3. Overall Assessment**\nThe Overall assessment score is an explicit recommendation for the outcome of this paper, if it were committed to an *ACL venue. This is a composite score reflecting your assessment of soundness, excitement, and also other factors like novelty and impact."],"durationSeconds":12.897666344999998}}
